# The data files are written with CRLF terminators, deliberately — RFC 4180 says so and
# every spreadsheet accepts it. Without this line git would normalise them to LF on
# commit (if `core.autocrlf` is set anywhere), and the file in the repository would stop
# being byte-identical to the file the scraper produces — which is exactly the property
# the daily job relies on to decide there is nothing to commit.
data/**/*.csv -text

# The captured page fixture is gzipped, so it is binary and must not be diffed as text.
tests/fixtures/*.gz binary
